Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:

$$
u=\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|}
$$

First, let's compute the sum:

$$
\begin{aligned}
2a+b &= 2\cdot \begin{bmatrix}0 \\ -2\end{bmatrix}+\begin{bmatrix}2 \\ 13\end{bmatrix} \\
&= \begin{bmatrix}0 \\ -4\end{bmatrix}+\begin{bmatrix}2 \\ 13\end{bmatrix} \\
&= \begin{bmatrix}0+(2) \\ (-4)+(13)\end{bmatrix} \\
&= \begin{bmatrix}2 \\ 9\end{bmatrix}
\end{aligned}
$$

Using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get

$$
\begin{aligned}
|2a+b| &= \sqrt{(2)^2+(9)^2} \\
&= \sqrt{85} \\
&= \sqrt{85}
\end{aligned}
$$

Finally, we divide $2a+b$ by its length and get the following unit vector:

$$
\begin{aligned}
u &= \frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|} \\
&= \frac{1}{\sqrt{85}}\cdot (2a+b) \\
&= \frac{1}{\sqrt{85}}\cdot \begin{bmatrix}2 \\ 9\end{bmatrix} \\
&= \begin{bmatrix}\frac{2 \sqrt{85}}{85} \\ \frac{9 \sqrt{85}}{85}\end{bmatrix}
\end{aligned}
$$

